utor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, the fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm that change, and post-restart export, symlink defense, data integrity, cleanup, platform, and node health were demonstrated.","limitations":["Cleanup was directly tested after normal completion and a final-rename failure, but no signal-termination test was captured; signal cleanup is supported by inspection of the installed traps.","Lifecycle snapshots provide bounded platform, service, socket, package, and /tmp observations rather than a complete filesystem inventory; final project state and persistence therefore rely on the captured executor probes."]}
